{"module":"colonizers","voice":"male","duration":389.1,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Los colonizadores: Portugal, España, Gran Bretaña y el sistema imperial","start":0.0,"end":5.49,"words":[[0.0,0.22],[0.22,1.27],[1.53,2.21],[2.47,2.99],[3.26,3.56],[3.56,4.08],[4.08,4.15],[4.15,4.3],[4.3,4.83],[4.83,5.43]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Colón fue una persona dentro de un sistema que funcionó durante cuatro siglos.","start":6.29,"end":11.3,"words":[[6.32,6.67],[6.67,6.88],[6.88,7.08],[7.08,7.57],[7.57,7.98],[7.98,8.12],[8.12,8.26],[8.26,8.75],[8.75,8.88],[8.88,9.44],[9.44,9.92],[9.92,10.34],[10.34,10.82]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Cada imperio añadió una pieza a la maquinaria: el comercio, la teoría legal, el código de plantación, las categorías raciales.","start":11.65,"end":20.67,"words":[[11.68,11.96],[11.96,12.45],[12.45,12.87],[12.87,13.08],[13.08,13.43],[13.43,13.5],[13.5,13.64],[13.64,14.35],[14.59,14.73],[14.73,15.37],[15.61,15.75],[15.75,16.25],[16.25,16.67],[16.91,17.05],[17.05,17.48],[17.48,17.62],[17.62,18.39],[18.64,18.85],[18.85,19.62],[19.62,20.25]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Juntos construyeron el mundo al que la Ley CAREN todavía responde.","start":21.02,"end":25.53,"words":[[21.06,21.48],[21.48,22.32],[22.32,22.46],[22.46,22.81],[22.81,22.95],[22.95,23.09],[23.09,23.23],[23.23,23.44],[23.44,23.79],[23.79,24.35],[24.35,24.99]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Portugal abre la trata atlántica","start":25.88,"end":28.32,"words":[[25.92,26.55],[26.55,26.86],[26.86,27.02],[27.02,27.41],[27.41,28.12]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1444, en Lagos (Portugal), unos 235 africanos cautivos fueron repartidos y vendidos en una plaza pública, un hecho que el cronista real Gomes Eanes de Zurara describió en detalle.","start":29.02,"end":44.68,"words":[[29.05,29.2],[29.2,31.55],[31.81,31.96],[31.96,32.33],[32.33,32.99],[33.25,33.54],[33.54,35.24],[35.24,35.9],[35.9,36.49],[36.49,36.93],[36.93,37.67],[37.67,37.74],[37.74,38.33],[38.33,38.48],[38.48,38.7],[38.7,39.07],[39.07,39.65],[39.91,40.06],[40.06,40.35],[40.35,40.5],[40.5,40.65],[40.65,41.24],[41.24,41.53],[41.53,41.9],[41.9,42.27],[42.27,42.42],[42.42,42.86],[42.86,43.52],[43.52,43.67],[43.67,44.26]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Portugal construyó el castillo de Elmina en 1482 y comerció a lo largo de la costa africana.","start":45.03,"end":52.52,"words":[[45.05,45.63],[45.63,46.27],[46.27,46.42],[46.42,46.99],[46.99,47.14],[47.14,47.57],[47.57,47.71],[47.71,49.65],[49.65,49.72],[49.72,50.3],[50.3,50.37],[50.37,50.51],[50.51,50.87],[50.87,51.02],[51.02,51.16],[51.16,51.52],[51.52,52.17]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En 1526, el rey Afonso I del Congo, él mismo cristiano y aliado de Portugal, escribió al rey de Portugal para protestar porque los traficantes secuestraban a su pueblo, “incluso a nobles e hijos de nobles”.","start":52.87,"end":67.7,"words":[[52.89,53.04],[53.04,54.7],[54.95,55.1],[55.1,55.32],[55.32,55.75],[55.75,55.82],[55.82,56.04],[56.04,56.47],[56.73,56.87],[56.87,57.23],[57.23,57.89],[57.89,57.96],[57.96,58.39],[58.39,58.54],[58.54,59.19],[59.44,60.02],[60.02,60.17],[60.17,60.38],[60.38,60.53],[60.53,61.11],[61.11,61.4],[61.4,62.05],[62.05,62.41],[62.41,62.63],[62.63,63.42],[63.42,64.29],[64.29,64.36],[64.36,64.51],[64.51,65.02],[65.27,65.78],[65.78,65.85],[65.85,66.28],[66.28,66.35],[66.35,66.64],[66.64,66.79],[66.79,67.3]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Los barcos portugueses y brasileños llevaron a través del Atlántico a unos 5.8 millones de africanos, más que cualquier otra nación.","start":68.05,"end":77.38,"words":[[68.11,68.32],[68.32,68.76],[68.76,69.48],[69.48,69.55],[69.55,70.27],[70.27,70.78],[70.78,70.85],[70.85,71.28],[71.28,71.5],[71.5,72.15],[72.15,72.22],[72.22,72.51],[72.51,73.52],[73.52,74.1],[74.1,74.25],[74.25,74.97],[75.22,75.44],[75.44,75.58],[75.58,76.16],[76.16,76.45],[76.45,76.95]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Brasil fue el mayor destino y el último país de América en abolir la esclavitud, en 1888.","start":77.73,"end":85.92,"words":[[77.76,78.23],[78.23,78.46],[78.46,78.62],[78.62,79.01],[79.01,79.56],[79.56,79.64],[79.64,79.79],[79.79,80.26],[80.26,80.57],[80.57,80.73],[80.73,81.28],[81.28,81.43],[81.43,81.9],[81.9,82.06],[82.06,82.92],[83.19,83.35],[83.35,85.53]]},{"el":"h1","text":"España se pregunta si los indígenas son plenamente humanos","start":86.82,"end":90.58,"words":[[86.84,87.29],[87.29,87.44],[87.44,88.04],[88.04,88.19],[88.19,88.41],[88.41,89.08],[89.08,89.31],[89.31,90.06],[90.06,90.51]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Desde 1513, los conquistadores españoles leían en voz alta el Requerimiento, en español, a pueblos que no podían entenderlo, exigiendo sumisión a la Corona y a la Iglesia y declarando que cualquier muerte resultante sería culpa de ellos.","start":91.28,"end":108.77,"words":[[91.3,91.68],[91.68,93.03],[93.3,93.53],[93.53,94.51],[94.51,95.19],[95.19,95.64],[95.64,95.79],[95.79,96.02],[96.02,96.32],[96.32,96.47],[96.47,97.45],[97.72,97.87],[97.87,98.47],[98.73,98.81],[98.81,99.34],[99.34,99.49],[99.49,99.64],[99.64,100.17],[100.17,101.0],[101.26,102.02],[102.02,102.62],[102.62,102.7],[102.7,102.85],[102.85,103.3],[103.3,103.38],[103.38,103.45],[103.45,103.6],[103.6,104.13],[104.13,104.21],[104.21,104.96],[104.96,105.11],[105.11,105.72],[105.72,106.17],[106.17,106.93],[106.93,107.38],[107.38,107.76],[107.76,107.91],[107.91,108.36]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los indígenas eran asignados a españoles como trabajadores forzados bajo la encomienda.","start":109.12,"end":114.98,"words":[[109.14,109.36],[109.36,110.01],[110.01,110.3],[110.3,110.95],[110.95,111.02],[111.02,111.67],[111.67,111.95],[111.95,112.82],[112.82,113.4],[113.4,113.68],[113.68,113.83],[113.83,114.62]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Bartolomé de las Casas, antiguo encomendero convertido en fraile, pasó cincuenta años denunciándola; las Leyes Nuevas de 1542 la limitaron.","start":115.33,"end":125.32,"words":[[115.35,115.92],[115.92,116.05],[116.05,116.24],[116.24,116.62],[116.85,117.29],[117.29,118.0],[118.0,118.64],[118.64,118.76],[118.76,119.21],[119.44,119.69],[119.69,120.27],[120.27,120.52],[120.52,121.42],[121.64,121.83],[121.83,122.15],[122.15,122.54],[122.54,122.66],[122.66,124.2],[124.2,124.32],[124.32,124.96]]},{"el":"s1","text":"En la Junta de Valladolid (1550–51), Las Casas discutió con Juan Ginés de Sepúlveda, quien sostenía, citando a Aristóteles, que los indígenas eran “siervos por naturaleza”.","start":125.67,"end":139.29,"words":[[125.71,125.85],[125.85,126.0],[126.0,126.35],[126.35,126.49],[126.49,127.2],[127.2,129.83],[130.08,130.29],[130.29,130.65],[130.65,131.22],[131.22,131.43],[131.43,131.72],[131.72,132.07],[132.07,132.21],[132.21,132.92],[133.17,133.46],[133.46,134.17],[134.42,134.91],[134.91,134.98],[134.98,135.84],[136.08,136.23],[136.23,136.44],[136.44,137.08],[137.08,137.36],[137.36,137.86],[137.86,138.07],[138.07,138.86]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Más tarde, las colonias españolas clasificaron a las personas en decenas de castas de ascendencia mixta, registradas en pinturas oficiales.","start":139.64,"end":149.98,"words":[[139.69,139.92],[139.92,140.39],[140.66,140.9],[140.9,141.52],[141.52,142.22],[142.22,143.15],[143.15,143.23],[143.23,143.46],[143.46,144.08],[144.08,144.24],[144.24,144.78],[144.78,144.94],[144.94,145.41],[145.41,145.56],[145.56,146.34],[146.34,146.88],[147.16,148.01],[148.01,148.17],[148.17,148.79],[148.79,149.57]]},{"el":"h2","text":"¿Dónde empezó la “raza”?","start":150.88,"end":152.86,"words":[[150.91,151.23],[151.23,151.6],[151.6,151.72],[151.72,152.03]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Algunos historiadores rastrean la raza moderna hasta los estatutos españoles de limpieza de sangre, que desde el siglo XV excluían de ciertos cargos a personas con antepasados judíos o musulmanes incluso después de convertirse, haciendo de la ascendencia, y no de la fe, la prueba.","start":153.56,"end":171.93,"words":[[153.58,154.08],[154.08,154.93],[154.93,155.51],[155.51,155.65],[155.65,155.93],[155.93,156.43],[156.43,156.72],[156.72,156.93],[156.93,157.57],[157.57,158.22],[158.22,158.36],[158.36,158.93],[158.93,159.07],[159.07,159.57],[159.82,159.96],[159.96,160.32],[160.32,160.46],[160.46,160.82],[160.82,161.18],[161.18,161.89],[161.89,162.03],[162.03,162.53],[162.53,162.96],[162.96,163.03],[163.03,163.6],[163.6,163.82],[163.82,164.6],[164.6,165.1],[165.1,165.17],[165.17,165.89],[165.89,166.39],[166.39,166.89],[166.89,167.03],[167.03,167.89],[168.14,168.63],[168.63,168.78],[168.78,168.92],[168.92,169.7],[169.95,170.03],[170.03,170.17],[170.17,170.31],[170.31,170.45],[170.45,170.67],[170.92,171.06],[171.06,171.56]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Otros ven surgir la raza sobre todo de la esclavitud atlántica y del derecho colonial inglés.","start":172.28,"end":178.86,"words":[[172.28,172.67],[172.67,172.91],[172.91,173.38],[173.38,173.54],[173.54,173.86],[173.86,174.25],[174.25,174.57],[174.57,174.73],[174.73,174.89],[174.89,175.68],[175.68,176.39],[176.39,176.47],[176.47,176.71],[176.71,177.26],[177.26,177.89],[177.89,178.45]]},{"el":"s2","text":"La mayoría coincide en que se formó entre 1450 y 1700, que es el argumento del módulo “Antes de la raza”.","start":179.21,"end":188.33,"words":[[179.23,179.38],[179.38,179.97],[179.97,180.56],[180.56,180.71],[180.71,180.86],[180.86,181.01],[181.01,181.38],[181.38,181.75],[181.75,183.61],[183.61,183.68],[183.68,184.8],[185.06,185.2],[185.2,185.35],[185.35,185.5],[185.5,186.17],[186.17,186.39],[186.39,186.84],[186.84,187.21],[187.21,187.36],[187.36,187.51],[187.51,187.88]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Gran Bretaña escribe el código de plantación","start":189.23,"end":192.37,"words":[[189.26,189.58],[189.58,190.14],[190.14,190.71],[190.71,190.87],[190.87,191.35],[191.35,191.51],[191.51,192.31]]},{"el":"s3","text":"John Hawkins encabezó los primeros viajes esclavistas de Inglaterra en la década de 1560, más tarde con el respaldo de la reina Isabel I.","start":193.07,"end":203.04,"words":[[193.09,193.31],[193.31,193.75],[193.75,194.34],[194.34,194.57],[194.57,195.16],[195.16,195.6],[195.6,196.41],[196.41,196.56],[196.56,197.23],[197.23,197.37],[197.37,197.52],[197.52,197.96],[197.96,198.11],[198.11,199.59],[199.85,200.07],[200.07,200.44],[200.44,200.66],[200.66,200.81],[200.81,201.4],[201.4,201.55],[201.55,201.7],[201.7,202.07],[202.07,202.51],[202.51,202.66]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Royal African Company, fundada bajo el futuro Jacobo II, transportó más africanos esclavizados que cualquier otra compañía; a muchos los marcaban con “DY” por el duque de York.","start":203.39,"end":216.43,"words":[[203.41,203.57],[203.57,203.97],[203.97,204.52],[204.52,205.15],[205.43,205.98],[205.98,206.3],[206.3,206.46],[206.46,206.93],[206.93,207.41],[207.41,207.73],[208.0,208.79],[208.79,209.03],[209.03,209.74],[209.74,210.69],[210.69,210.85],[210.85,211.48],[211.48,211.8],[211.8,212.59],[212.87,212.95],[212.95,213.42],[213.42,213.66],[213.66,214.29],[214.29,214.53],[214.53,214.69],[214.69,214.93],[214.93,215.09],[215.09,215.4],[215.4,215.56],[215.56,215.96]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El código de esclavos de Barbados de 1661 se convirtió en el modelo de los de Jamaica y Carolina del Sur.","start":216.78,"end":224.96,"words":[[216.78,216.93],[216.93,217.36],[217.36,217.51],[217.51,218.1],[218.1,218.24],[218.24,218.83],[218.83,218.97],[218.97,220.88],[220.88,221.02],[221.02,221.68],[221.68,221.83],[221.83,221.97],[221.97,222.41],[222.41,222.56],[222.56,222.78],[222.78,222.92],[222.92,223.44],[223.44,223.51],[223.51,224.09],[224.09,224.31],[224.31,224.61]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Los barcos británicos llevaron en total a unos 3.2 millones de africanos.","start":225.31,"end":230.92,"words":[[225.36,225.58],[225.58,226.02],[226.02,226.74],[226.74,227.25],[227.25,227.39],[227.39,227.76],[227.76,227.83],[227.83,228.12],[228.12,228.99],[228.99,229.57],[229.57,229.71],[229.71,230.44]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En 1781, la tripulación del barco negrero Zong arrojó por la borda a unos 130 cautivos, y los dueños demandaron a sus aseguradoras por la pérdida como si fuera “carga”.","start":231.27,"end":244.41,"words":[[231.31,231.46],[231.46,233.42],[233.68,233.83],[233.83,234.63],[234.63,234.85],[234.85,235.21],[235.21,235.72],[235.72,235.94],[235.94,236.3],[236.3,236.52],[236.52,236.67],[236.67,237.03],[237.03,237.1],[237.1,237.4],[237.4,238.34],[238.34,239.0],[239.25,239.33],[239.33,239.54],[239.54,239.98],[239.98,240.71],[240.71,240.78],[240.78,241.0],[241.0,241.88],[241.88,242.09],[242.09,242.24],[242.24,242.75],[242.75,243.04],[243.04,243.19],[243.19,243.55],[243.55,243.99]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Los primeros africanos en la Virginia inglesa llegaron en 1619 a bordo del White Lion, un corsario inglés que los había capturado de un barco portugués que transportaba cautivos de Angola.","start":244.76,"end":258.07,"words":[[244.78,245.0],[245.0,245.59],[245.59,246.24],[246.24,246.39],[246.39,246.53],[246.53,247.11],[247.11,247.62],[247.62,248.13],[248.13,248.28],[248.28,250.03],[250.03,250.1],[250.1,250.46],[250.46,250.68],[250.68,250.97],[250.97,251.41],[251.67,251.81],[251.81,252.39],[252.39,252.83],[252.83,252.98],[252.98,253.2],[253.2,253.56],[253.56,254.21],[254.21,254.36],[254.36,254.51],[254.51,254.87],[254.87,255.45],[255.45,255.6],[255.6,256.47],[256.47,257.05],[257.05,257.2],[257.2,257.71]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Francia y los Países Bajos","start":258.97,"end":261.21,"words":[[258.99,259.67],[259.67,259.77],[259.77,260.06],[260.06,260.65],[260.65,261.13]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Compañía Neerlandesa de las Indias Occidentales comerció africanos esclavizados hacia América y usó mano de obra esclavizada en Nueva Ámsterdam (Nueva York).","start":261.91,"end":273.33,"words":[[261.92,262.08],[262.08,262.8],[262.8,263.68],[263.68,263.84],[263.84,264.08],[264.08,264.56],[264.56,265.52],[265.52,266.15],[266.15,266.87],[266.87,267.83],[267.83,268.15],[268.15,268.71],[268.71,268.79],[268.79,269.03],[269.03,269.35],[269.35,269.51],[269.51,269.83],[269.83,270.71],[270.71,270.87],[270.87,271.27],[271.27,271.99],[271.99,272.39],[272.39,272.79]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Code Noir de Francia (1685) regía sus colonias; Saint-Domingue, hoy Haití, se convirtió en la colonia más rentable del mundo gracias al trabajo de africanos esclavizados, hasta que derrocaron a los franceses (ver “Antes de la raza” y “Un sistema mundial”).","start":273.68,"end":292.27,"words":[[273.69,273.84],[273.84,274.13],[274.13,274.43],[274.43,274.57],[274.57,275.09],[275.09,277.07],[277.33,277.77],[277.77,277.99],[277.99,278.65],[278.9,279.86],[280.11,280.26],[280.26,280.63],[280.88,281.03],[281.03,281.69],[281.69,281.84],[281.84,281.98],[281.98,282.5],[282.5,282.72],[282.72,283.3],[283.3,283.52],[283.52,283.89],[283.89,284.4],[284.4,284.55],[284.55,285.06],[285.06,285.21],[285.21,285.87],[285.87,286.82],[287.08,287.37],[287.37,287.52],[287.52,288.18],[288.18,288.25],[288.25,288.47],[288.47,289.13],[289.13,289.35],[289.35,289.72],[289.72,289.87],[289.87,290.01],[290.01,290.31],[290.31,290.38],[290.38,290.53],[290.53,291.04],[291.04,291.63]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Estados Unidos se convierte en imperio","start":293.17,"end":295.76,"words":[[293.19,293.72],[293.72,294.17],[294.17,294.32],[294.32,294.99],[294.99,295.14],[295.14,295.67]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En 1893, empresarios estadounidenses respaldados por marines de EE. UU. derrocaron a la reina Liliʻuokalani de Hawái; el Congreso pidió perdón formalmente en 1993.","start":296.46,"end":313.01,"words":[[296.49,296.64],[296.64,298.6],[298.85,299.65],[299.65,300.74],[300.74,301.54],[301.54,301.76],[301.76,302.26],[302.26,302.41],[302.41,302.63],[302.99,303.21],[303.57,304.22],[304.22,304.3],[304.3,304.44],[304.44,304.81],[304.81,307.42],[307.42,307.56],[307.56,307.93],[308.18,308.33],[308.33,308.91],[308.91,309.27],[309.27,309.71],[309.71,310.51],[310.51,310.65],[310.65,312.61]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Después de 1898, EE. UU. tomó Puerto Rico, Guam y Filipinas.","start":313.36,"end":320.03,"words":[[313.39,313.87],[313.87,314.0],[314.0,315.93],[316.17,316.38],[316.72,316.93],[317.27,317.55],[317.55,317.96],[317.96,318.3],[318.54,318.82],[318.82,318.89],[318.89,319.58]]},{"el":"s5","text":"El poema de Rudyard Kipling “La carga del hombre blanco” (1899) instaba a los estadounidenses a gobernar Filipinas, donde una guerra contra los independentistas mató a cientos de miles de filipinos según la mayoría de las estimaciones.","start":320.38,"end":336.0,"words":[[320.38,320.52],[320.52,320.86],[320.86,321.0],[321.0,321.48],[321.48,321.89],[321.89,322.03],[322.03,322.38],[322.38,322.58],[322.58,322.93],[322.93,323.34],[323.34,325.2],[325.44,325.92],[325.92,325.99],[325.99,326.19],[326.19,327.23],[327.23,327.29],[327.29,327.84],[327.84,328.53],[328.77,329.12],[329.12,329.32],[329.32,329.6],[329.6,330.01],[330.01,330.22],[330.22,331.32],[331.32,331.59],[331.59,331.66],[331.66,332.14],[332.14,332.28],[332.28,332.63],[332.63,332.76],[332.76,333.38],[333.38,333.73],[333.73,333.86],[333.86,334.41],[334.41,334.55],[334.55,334.76],[334.76,335.65]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En los Casos Insulares (1901), la Corte Suprema llamó a Puerto Rico “extranjero … en un sentido doméstico”; sus residentes son ciudadanos de EE. UU. que todavía no pueden votar por el presidente.","start":336.35,"end":350.33,"words":[[336.39,336.53],[336.53,336.75],[336.75,337.1],[337.1,337.75],[337.75,339.04],[339.29,339.44],[339.44,339.8],[339.8,340.3],[340.3,340.59],[340.59,340.66],[340.66,341.09],[341.09,341.38],[341.38,342.17],[342.17,342.24],[342.24,342.38],[342.38,342.53],[342.53,343.03],[343.03,343.75],[344.0,344.21],[344.21,344.93],[344.93,345.15],[345.15,345.86],[345.86,346.01],[346.01,346.22],[346.58,346.8],[347.16,347.3],[347.3,347.87],[347.87,348.02],[348.02,348.45],[348.45,348.81],[348.81,349.02],[349.02,349.17],[349.17,349.96]]},{"el":"h6","text":"El patrón común","start":351.23,"end":352.83,"words":[[351.26,351.46],[351.46,352.08],[352.08,352.6]]},{"el":"s6","text":"A lo largo de cinco siglos y en todos los imperios aparecen las mismas herramientas: reclamar la tierra (el “descubrimiento”), clasificar a las personas por ascendencia o color, tomar su trabajo, escribirlo en la ley, justificarlo con la religión y luego con la ciencia, y dividir a los colonizados entre sí.","start":353.53,"end":372.65,"words":[[353.53,353.6],[353.6,353.74],[353.74,354.08],[354.08,354.22],[354.22,354.57],[354.57,354.98],[354.98,355.05],[355.05,355.19],[355.19,355.54],[355.54,355.74],[355.74,356.3],[356.3,356.85],[356.85,357.06],[357.06,357.48],[357.48,358.24],[358.48,359.04],[359.04,359.18],[359.18,359.52],[359.52,359.66],[359.66,360.7],[360.94,361.64],[361.64,361.7],[361.7,361.91],[361.91,362.47],[362.47,362.67],[362.67,363.37],[363.37,363.44],[363.44,363.85],[364.1,364.44],[364.44,364.58],[364.58,365.13],[365.38,366.07],[366.07,366.21],[366.21,366.35],[366.35,366.62],[366.87,367.7],[367.7,367.91],[367.91,368.05],[368.05,368.6],[368.6,368.67],[368.67,369.02],[369.02,369.22],[369.22,369.36],[369.36,369.92],[370.16,370.23],[370.23,370.71],[370.71,370.78],[370.78,370.99],[370.99,371.75],[371.75,372.1],[372.1,372.31]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La resistencia también aparece en todas partes, desde el rey del Congo hasta los revolucionarios de Haití y la reina de Hawái.","start":373.0,"end":381.88,"words":[[373.03,373.19],[373.19,374.07],[374.07,374.63],[374.63,375.18],[375.18,375.34],[375.34,375.74],[375.74,376.3],[376.58,376.98],[376.98,377.14],[377.14,377.38],[377.38,377.62],[377.62,378.02],[378.02,378.34],[378.34,378.58],[378.58,379.77],[379.77,379.93],[379.93,380.25],[380.25,380.33],[380.33,380.49],[380.49,380.89],[380.89,381.05],[381.05,381.45]]},{"el":"s6","text":"El resto de los módulos de Aprende sigue estas herramientas dentro de las instituciones estadounidenses.","start":382.23,"end":388.23,"words":[[382.26,382.39],[382.39,382.71],[382.71,382.84],[382.84,383.03],[383.03,383.48],[383.48,383.61],[383.61,384.06],[384.06,384.31],[384.31,384.64],[384.64,385.28],[385.28,385.66],[385.66,385.79],[385.79,385.98],[385.98,386.82],[386.82,387.85]]}],"audio":"https://carenactmedia.blob.core.windows.net/audio/es/colonizers.male.97da1fe85e.mp3","bytes":1556793,"sha256":"97da1fe85e4612d36588537977f3bf1e684127a9e6a1e68a7d6f74f505b4aa22"}